# Result tables are generated per campaign, by
# `uv run python -m report render <campaign dir>` (run in the superproject's
# `benchmark/`), from a result store that lives outside this repository
# (`/data/bench/results/<campaign>/`). They are ignored by default so that a
# dev, smoke or pilot campaign cannot drift into the manuscript tree unnoticed.
#
# Each table is written three ways: `results-<campaign>-<table>.typ`, which
# the thesis includes, the `.table.json` it loads, and a `.tex` kept only
# until the LaTeX build is retired. `report render` also writes pgfplots
# sources under `figures/`; Typst cannot use them.
#
# `figures/` also receives the figures the thesis does include: `make figures`
# renders them from data and scripts tracked here (e.g. `dimensioning/`), and
# `make build` runs it first, locally and in CI. They are never committed.
#
# When a campaign is the one the thesis quotes, commit its Typst tables
# deliberately, from the root of this repository:
#     git add -f generated/results-<campaign>-*.typ generated/results-<campaign>-*.table.json
# Do not commit the `.tex` tables or `figures/`: the Typst thesis reads
# neither.
#
# `deviations.*` and `methods-provenance.*` (`.typ`, `.table.json`, `.tex`) are
# NOT ignored: `uv run deviations render` generates them from the manifest and
# the forks, which are in the superproject, so they are reproducible by anyone
# who clones it.
results-*
figures/
